/10.1016/s0301-0082(02)00009-6</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Moore KA, Kohno T, Karchewski LA, Scholz J, Baba H, Woolf CJ (2002) Partial peripheral nerve injury promotes a selective loss of GABAergic inhibition in the superficial dorsal horn of the spinal cord. J neuroscience: official J Soc Neurosci 22(15):6724&#x2013;6731. https://doi.org/10.1523/jneurosci.22-15-06724.2002</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Petitjean H, Pawlowski SA, Fraine SL, Sharif B, Hamad D, Fatima T, Berg J, Brown CM, Jan LY, Ribeiro-da-Silva A et al (2015) Dorsal Horn Parvalbumin Neurons Are Gate-Keepers of Touch-Evoked Pain after Nerve Injury. Cell Rep 13(6):1246&#x2013;1257. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2015.09.080</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Kong C, Du J, Bu H, Huang C, Xu F, Ren H (2020) LncRNA KCNA2-AS regulates spinal astrocyte activation through STAT3 to affect postherpetic neuralgia. Mol Med (Cambridge Mass) 26(1):113. https://doi.org/10.1186/s10020-020-00232-9</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Bjelland I, Dahl AA, Haug TT, Neckelmann D (2002) The validity of the Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale. An updated literature review. J Psychosom Res 52(2):69&#x2013;77. https://doi.org/10.1016/s0022-3999(01)00296-3</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Kroenke K, Spitzer RL, Williams JB (2001) The PHQ-9: validity of a brief depression severity measure. J Gen Intern Med 16(9):606&#x2013;613. https://doi.org/10.1046/j.1525-1497.2001.016009606.x</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Melzack R (1975) The McGill Pain Questionnaire: major properties and scoring methods. Pain 1(3):277&#x2013;299. https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-3959(75)90044-5</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Bouhassira D, Attal N, Alchaar H, Boureau F, Brochet B, Bruxelle J, Cunin G, Fermanian J, Ginies P, Grun-Overdyking A et al (2005) Comparison of pain syndromes associated with nervous or somatic lesions and development of a new neuropathic pain diagnostic questionnaire (DN4). Pain 114(1&#x2013;2):29&#x2013;36. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pain.2004.12.010</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Freynhagen R, Baron R, Gockel U, T&#xf6;lle TR (2006) painDETECT: a new screening questionnaire to identify neuropathic components in patients with back pain. Curr Med Res Opin 22(10):1911&#x2013;1920. https://doi.org/10.1185/030079906x132488</Citation></Reference></ReferenceList></PubmedData></PubmedArticle><PubmedArticle><MedlineCitation Status="MEDLINE" Owner="NLM" IndexingMethod="Automated"><PMID Version="1">41832365</PMID><DateCompleted><Year>2026</Year><Month>03</Month><Day>15</Day></DateCompleted><DateRevised><Year>2026</Year><Month>03</Month><Day>15</Day></DateRevised><Article PubModel="Electronic"><Journal><ISSN IssnType="Electronic">1865-5785</ISSN><JournalIssue CitedMedium="Internet"><Volume>19</Volume><Issue>1</Issue><PubDate><Year>2026</Year><Month>Mar</Month><Day>14</Day></PubDate></JournalIssue><Title>Journal of hematopathology</Title><ISOAbbreviation>J Hematop</ISOAbbreviation></Journal><ArticleTitle>Primary diffuse large B-cell lymphoma of cauda equina: a rare and challenging diagnosis.</ArticleTitle><ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">11</ELocationID><ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12308-026-00689-3</ELocationID><Abstract><AbstractText>Primary diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) of cauda equina is a very rare manifestation of neurolymphomatosis. A 52-year-old female presented with progressive symptoms of left lower extremity burning sensation. After initial conservative management with no improvement, MRI of the lumbosacral spine showed pathologic enhancement and thickening of cauda equina nerve roots. Examination of cerebrospinal fluid, coupled with flow cytometry, was diagnostic of DLBCL. Clinicians and pathologists should be aware of this unusual and challenging clinical presentation of DLBCL.</AbstractText><CopyrightInformation>&#xa9; 2026. The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Springer-Verlag GmbH Germany, part of Springer Nature.</CopyrightInformation></Abstract><AuthorList CompleteYN="Y"><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Pikivaca</LastName><ForeName>Tamara</ForeName><Initials>T</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Department of Pathology and Cytology, University Hospital Centre Zagreb, Zagreb, Croatia.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Rudolf</LastName><ForeName>Mark A</ForeName><Initials>MA</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Department of Pathology, University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, MI, USA.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Perry</LastName><ForeName>Anamarija M</ForeName><Initials>AM</Initials><Identifier Source="ORCID">0000-0002-5700-2141</Identifier><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Department of Pathology, University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, MI, USA. anaperry@med.umich.edu.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Section of Hematopathology, Department of Pathology, University of Michigan, North Campus Research Complex, 2800 Plymouth Road, Bldg. 36, Ann Arbor, MI, 48109, USA. anaperry@med.umich.edu.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author></AuthorList><Language>eng</Language><PublicationTypeList><PublicationType UI="D016428">Journal Article</PublicationType><PublicationType UI="D002363">Case Reports</PublicationType></PublicationTypeList><ArticleDate DateType="Electronic"><Year>2026</Year><Month>03</Month><Day>14</Day></ArticleDate></Article><MedlineJournalInfo><Country>Germany</Country><MedlineTA>J Hematop</MedlineTA><NlmUniqueID>101491976</NlmUniqueID><ISSNLinking>1865-5785</ISSNLinking></MedlineJournalInfo><CitationSubset>IM</CitationSubset><MeshHeadingList><MeshHeading><DescriptorName UI="D006801" MajorTopicYN="N">Humans</DescriptorName></MeshHeading><MeshHeading><DescriptorName UI="D005260" MajorTopicYN="N">Female</DescriptorName></MeshHeading><MeshHeading><DescriptorName UI="D016403" MajorTopicYN="Y">Lymphoma, Large B-Cell, Diffuse</Descr