 AbbVie, Amgen and Biohaven. Anna Cirkel declares that there are no conflicts of interest. Hartmut G&#xf6;bel has served on scientific advisory boards for Organon, Schwabe, Novartis, Teva, Lundbeck, Lilly, and AbbVie. He has received honoraria for lectures and educational activities from Novartis, Teva, Lundbeck, Lilly, and AbbVie. He has been involved in research projects and/or the conduct of clinical trials supported by Novartis, Teva, Lundbeck, AbbVie, Amgen, Biohaven, Charit&#xe9;, and the University of Essen.</CoiStatement></MedlineCitation><PubmedData><History><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="received"><Year>2026</Year><Month>2</Month><Day>12</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="revised"><Year>2026</Year><Month>2</Month><Day>27</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="accepted"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>3</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="medline"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>14</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>33</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pubmed"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>14</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>32</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="entrez"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>14</Day><Hour>1</Hour><Minute>1</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pmc-release"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>3</Day></PubMedPubDate></History><PublicationStatus>epublish</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">41827347</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.3390/jcm15051930</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pii">jcm15051930</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC12985913</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation>Eftekhari S., Salvatore C.A., Johansson S., Chen T.B., Zeng Z., Edvinsson L. Localization of CGRP, CGRP receptor, PACAP and glutamate in trigeminal ganglion. Relation to the blood-brain barrier. Brain Res. 2015;1600:93&#x2013;109. doi: 10.1016/j.brainres.2014.11.031.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.