 journal. The authors have no relevant conflicts of interest to declare.</CoiStatement></MedlineCitation><PubmedData><History><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="received"><Year>2025</Year><Month>8</Month><Day>7</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="accepted"><Year>2026</Year><Month>2</Month><Day>25</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="revised"><Year>2026</Year><Month>1</Month><Day>19</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="medline"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>14</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>33</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pubmed"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>14</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>33</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="entrez"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>14</Day><Hour>0</Hour><Minute>27</Minute></PubMedPubDate></History><PublicationStatus>aheadofprint</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">41826661</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/s41372-026-02618-9</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pii">10.1038/s41372-026-02618-9</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation>Volpe JJ. Neurology of the newborn. Major Probl Clin Pediatr. 1981;22:1&#x2013;648.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">7022034</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Lundgren EM, Cnattingius S, Jonsson B, Tuvemo T. Intellectual and psychological performance in males born small for gestational age with and without catch-up growth. Pediatr Res. 2001;50:91&#x2013;6.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">11420424</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1203/00006450-200107000-00017</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Rimol LM, Botellero VL, Bjuland KJ, L&#xf8;haugen GCC, Lydersen S, Evensen KAI, et al. Reduced white matter fractional anisotropy mediates cortical thickening in adults born preterm with very low birthweight. Neuroimage. 2019;188:217&#x2013;27.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">30502