MajorTopicYN="N">white matter</Keyword></KeywordList></MedlineCitation><PubmedData><History><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="revised"><Year>2025</Year><Month>12</Month><Day>23</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="received"><Year>2025</Year><Month>8</Month><Day>26</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="accepted"><Year>2026</Year><Month>1</Month><Day>12</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="medline"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>25</Day><Hour>12</Hour><Minute>49</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pubmed"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>25</Day><Hour>12</Hour><Minute>48</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="entrez"><Year>2026</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>25</Day><Hour>8</Hour><Minute>43</Minute></PubMedPubDate></History><PublicationStatus>ppublish</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">41879269</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1002/jimd.70148</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Title>References</Title><Reference><Citation>F. W. Verheijen, E. Verbeek, N. Aula, et&#xa0;al., &#x201c;A New Gene, Encoding an Anion Transporter, Is Mutated in Sialic Acid Storage Diseases,&#x201d; Nature Genetics 23 (1999): 462&#x2013;465.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>D. Adams and M. Wasserstein, &#x201c;Free Sialic Acid Storage Disorders,&#x201d; in GeneReviews, ed. M. P. Adam, H. H. Ardinger, R. A. Pagon, et&#xa0;al. (University of Washington, 2003).</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>P. Aula and W. A. Gahl, &#x201c;Disorders of Free Sialic Acid Storage,&#x201d; in The Online Metabolic and Molecular Bases of Inherited Disease, ed. D. L. Valle, S. Antonarakis, A. Ballabio, and A. L. Beaudet (McGraw&#x2010;Hill, 2019).</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>F. Valianpour, N. Abeling, M. Duran, J. Huijmans, and W. Kulik, &#x201c;Quantification of Free Sialic Acid in Urine by HPLC&#x2013;Electrospray Tandem Mass Spectrometry: A Tool for the Diagnosis of Sialic Acid Storage Disea